    "58998": {
      "label": "1",
      "explanation": "The text uses strong moral language to criticize the legal system: 'the rule of lawyers threatens our global competitiveness, denies Americans access to the quality of justice they deserve, and puts every small business one lawsuit away from bankruptcy.' The phrase 'quality of justice they deserve' is a clear moral claim about fairness and rights. The overall tone is a moral indictment of the system."
