      "explanation": "The text lists future professions, including 'doctors and nurses who heal and comfort the sick, the teachers who will educate the next generation, the leaders who transform government, the poets, artists, and writers who entertain and inspire.' This is a rhetorical celebration of various professions as noble and good. It attributes moral and social value (healing, comforting, educating, inspiring) to these roles, which is a form of moral rhetoric."
